cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite it as below."
title: "2D potential energy surface for H2 on Si(111) (VASP PBE-D3)"
abstract: >-
  Two-dimensional potential energy surface for an H2 molecule standing upright
  above a surface Si atom of a frozen Si(111) slab: 1159 VASP PBE-D3 single-point
  energies on a 29 x 40 grid of H-H distance and H height, a fitted surface
  (physical baseline plus Gaussian-process regression, analytic gradients) for
  dynamics and reaction-path work, and the scripts used to produce and analyse it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Khokhar
    given-names: Vikash
repository-code: "https://github.com/vkhokhar141/Si111-H2-PES"
url: "https://github.com/vkhokhar141/Si111-H2-PES"
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - potential energy surface
  - hydrogen
  - Si(111)
  - density functional theory
  - VASP
  - PBE-D3
  - Gaussian process regression
  - Eley-Rideal
